{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' CLAUDE.md && sed -n '1,320p' _ai_sessions/260731_1134_env-to-db-settings/workdir/260731_1136_design-doc.md && sed -n '1,320p' _ai_sessions/260731_1134_env-to-db-settings/workdir/260731_1136_chunk-plan.md\"","aggregated_output":"# CLAUDE.md — kidOS\n\nSingle-family web app, a calm fake-OS desktop (the \"bureau\") for one child:\ncalm illustrated read-aloud stories in French where the configured child hero\nstars, plus a \"Poser des calculs\" mini-app (posed column arithmetic, no LLM),\neach opening in its own window. TanStack Start + React 19.\nDeploys via Docker (Compose) and runs locally; the database is a local\nSQLite file under `DATA_DIR` (in Docker: the app-data volume) — no cloud\ndb, no db setup. No authentication — the compose\nfile binds to loopback only; exposing it further is the operator's problem.\n\n## THE NON-NEGOTIABLE CONSTRAINT\n\nThis is a CALM TOOL for a young child, NOT a game. NEVER add: score, note,\ntimer, \"bravo/gagné/perdu\", gamification, unlock, reward, streak,\nnotification, progress bar, %, quiz, evaluation, or any sense of\nstakes/performance. This overrides every generic \"good app\" instinct. The\ndesign test for any feature: \"does it add stakes, pressure, or dependence?\" If\nyes → don't.\n\n## Commands\n\n- `bun run dev` — dev server on port 3009\n- `bun run build` / `bun run start` — clean local run (start uses PORT=3009)\n- `bun run check-types` — tsc\n- `bun run lint` / `bun run lint:fix` — Biome, extending the ultracite\n  presets (core + react + tanstack); the deliberate opt-outs (jsx handlers,\n  bitwise in the seeded generator, module façades, route filenames) are\n  documented inline in `biome.jsonc` and win over the presets.\n- `bun run test` — golden assertion scripts (plain bun, no vitest):\n  `test:golden` pins prompt identity (text fragments + the segment-image\n  prompt builder, byte-identical); `test:coherence` pins the safety/structure\n  validators, the anti-\"doux\" repetition guard, the landing decrescendo, the\n  prompt builders and the zod schema key order (key order IS the JSON property\n  order sent to the model — a formatting pass must not reorder it), PLUS the\n  ENGLISH corpus branch (english-coherence.golden.ts: EN prompts/validators,\n  the word-boundary safety scan, EN schema key order = FR, the EN illustration\n  prompt byte-pinned, the no-lang default staying French);\n  `test:media` pins the media-store rules: blob-host derivation and the\n  read-back choke-point (allowlist in both modes, media-dir escape, bytes\n  round-trip);\n  `test:data-route` pins the `/data/$` media-serving route;\n  `test:reading-aids` pins the silent-letter/liaison annotator;\n  `test:operations` pins the posed-operations module (seeded generator,\n  layout geometry, palier ladder, énoncé templates in BOTH languages —\n  EN pool length/index alignment proved, EN pins = translation of the same\n  seeded draw, calm-wording scan fr AND en) and\n  the serie-session lifecycle (legacy bridge, authoritative purge,\n  resume/purge-on-mismatch, fingerprint round-trip, silent storage\n  degradation);\n  `test:bureau` pins the desktop layer's pure modules (window clamp incl.\n  the committed-position re-clamp `reclampCommitted`, session shape guard,\n  icon-selection state machine, childName↔hero identity match);\n  `test:i18n` pins the UI-locale module (fr↔en catalog key parity, the\n  calm-wording scan on BOTH catalogs, byte-identity of the relocated French\n  labels, per-locale branding incl. French elision / English possessive,\n  `normalizeLocale` strictness);\n  `test:routes` pins public-URL integrity of the `_bureau/` relocation (no\n  URL changed, no stale route id, /parents never under the layout) plus two\n  prose contracts: no `ssr:` option under `src/app/_bureau/**` and the\n  closed-session gate CALLED in exactly two files, never `__root`;\n  `test:db` pins the local-SQLite bootstrap (`file:` URL derivation +\n  env validations, real boot on a blank dir with all migrations applied,\n  idempotent restart, no spurious `.pre-migrate` snapshot, and the\n  Dockerfile contract — `drizzle/` shipped next to the server bundle).\n- Migrations AUTO-APPLY at app startup (`db/index.ts`, idempotent) — no\n  setup step. `db:generate` creates a new migration from schema edits;\n  `db:migrate` applies them manually (rarely needed); `db:push` is also\n  available for quick dev schema sync — but it syncs SCHEMA only and never\n  runs DATA migrations (e.g. 0010): never rely on it for a release whose\n  migration rewrites rows.\n- `bun run deploy` — `docker compose up -d --build` (see Nitro bullet; needs\n  `.env.production` + optionally `.env` for build-time `VITE_*` args).\n- Releases: 4-digit `VERSION` + `CHANGELOG.md` (French, Keep-a-Changelog\n  style); deferred work lives in `TODOS.md`.\n\n## Architecture\n\n- **Framework**: TanStack Start (file routes in `src/app/`; index (the\n  DESKTOP — see Bureau bullet) + aventure + calcul + bibliotheque (relocated\n  under the pathless layout `src/app/_bureau/`, public URLs unchanged) +\n  parents section, incl. /parents/calcul — /parents stays OUTSIDE the\n  desktop grammar).\n- **Bureau (the calm fake-OS frame)**: `/` renders the portrait screen OR\n  the desktop (3 icons, dblclick native + Enter — the \"Ouvrir\" fallback was\n  REMOVED by user decision 2026-07-22, single click only selects; \"Ranger\n  le bureau\" ritual) — the choice is 100% client (localStorage\n  `bureau:session`, shape-guarded, silent failure; pure modules in\n  `src/lib/bureau/`, golden-tested via `test:bureau`). The `_bureau` layout\n  wraps each mini-app in ONE window (`src/components/bureau/fenetre.tsx`):\n  ~85% viewport, drag by title bar only (@dnd-kit, clamp = title bar fully\n  visible, commit in left/top — NEVER a persistent transform, it would\n  offset /calcul's DragOverlay), reopen always centered, <lg fullscreen\n  without drag, print neutralized (`.bureau-fenetre` rules). CONTRACT: the\n  layout never sets `ssr` (Selective SSR is inherited down — an `ssr:false`\n  would silently make the mini-apps client-only; golden-pinned, no `ssr:`\n  option anywhere under `_bureau/`); the closed-session gate\n  lives at exactly TWO places (`_bureau` layout as an optimistic overlay +\n  `/`), never `__root` (else /parents and /data/$ would be gated). The\n  `__root` shell is route-aware: full-bleed for the desktop layer, the\n  `max-w-5xl` container is kept for /parents (the window frame provides the\n  container inside).\n- **Nitro**: `node-server` preset → builds a standalone `.output/server/\n  index.mjs` (traced deps included, native libsql binding too) that `bun run\n  start` and the Docker image both run. Deploy = `Dockerfile` (multi-stage:\n  `node:22-slim` build stage with the bun binary copied in from `oven/bun` —\n  bun only installs deps and runs scripts; vite/rolldown MUST run under real\n  node, because under bun `ws` resolves as a builtin and the bundle ships a\n  bare `import \"ws\"` that crashes the node runtime — `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1`\n  + `VITE_*` build args → `node:22-slim` runtime, port 3009) + `compose.yml` (loopback-bound port,\n  `app-data` volume on `/app/data`, secrets via `env_file: .env.production`).\n  Machine-specific compose changes go in a gitignored `compose.override.yml`,\n  never in `compose.yml`.\n- **DB**: local SQLite file (libSQL `file:` URL, default\n  `file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db`) via `@libsql/client` + Drizzle. `db/index.ts`\n  creates the parent dir, opens the client and AUTO-APPLIES drizzle\n  migrations at startup (skipped when `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION` is set, i.e.\n  during build; the Dockerfile ships `drizzle/` next to the server bundle\n  since the folder is resolved from the CWD). Persisted tables\n  (`src/server/db/schema.ts`): `stories`, `story_segments`, `places`,\n  `doudous`, `heroes`, `elements`, plus `math_skills` (migration 0009 ; the\n  DATA migration 0010, guarded/idempotent, rekeyed it) — one row per\n  ACTIVATED operation family (`calcul-pose:<famille>`, presence = activated),\n  each carrying that family's parent-chosen palier + the global série size\n  (copied on every row, read in canonical family order — settingsFromRows).\n  The `src/config/*.ts` files seed/back those\n  entity tables (editable via in-app CRUD at /parents). Coherence columns\n  (nullable, older rows fall back to prior behavior): `stories.story_arc`\n  (hidden \"fil rouge\" frozen at creation), `stories.visual_world` (story-level\n  illustration ambiance — time of day, season, weather, light — generated in\n  the SAME call as the arc) and `story_segments.scene_hint` (per-beat scene\n  description for the illustrator).\n- **UI language (multilang phase 1)**: the desktop SHELL is bilingual fr/en —\n  a PARENT setting (🌍 card on /parents), persisted in the `app_settings`\n  table (key `ui-language`), read ONLY by the `__root` loader\n  (`getUiLocaleFn`, never throws — DB down → \"fr\") and propagated via\n  `LocaleProvider`/`useMessages()` (`src/lib/i18n/`: typed catalogs\n  `messages/{fr,en}.ts`, pure `buildBranding`, `normalizeLocale`;\n  golden-tested via `test:i18n`). `<html lang>` and the tab title/description\n  follow. DISTINCT from `stories.lang` (per-story, frozen at creation) and\n  `DEFAULT_LANG` (server-side story default). Since phase 3 STORIES follow\n  the UI language at creation (the wizard passes the locale; `Lang` is now\n  \"fr\" | \"ru\" | \"en\"): the whole EN corpus (system/beat/arc prompts,\n  EN reading-level spec, forbidden/stakes lists, anti-tic soft/softly/gentle,\n  validator messages, EN beat/arc schemas with the SAME key order, EN image\n  fragments) lives in `src/server/providers/text/english.ts` — the FR/RU\n  path in dynamic.ts is byte-frozen and only BRANCHES there on lang===\"en\".\n  CRITICAL divergence: the EN safety scan is WORD-BOUNDARY, never substring\n  (\"war\" ⊂ \"warm\" would reject core cozy vocabulary; FR keeps its historical\n  substring scan). Reading aids (French phonics) are gated to\n  `story.lang === \"fr\"` (player + print: annotations off, toggles hidden);\n  the cursive font toggle stays in both. TTS voice map carries\n  en-US-AnaNeural. Since phase 4 the WHOLE UI is bilingual — the aventure\n  wizard/player chrome, bibliotheque, and every /parents page (entity pages,\n  the four CRUD forms via the shared `parents.formulaires` section, the\n  playground); templated aria-labels compose via `formatMessage`\n  (\"Modifier {label}\"). What stays family-language ON PURPOSE (decision D5):\n  entity DATA (heroes/places/elements/doudous labels + promptHints, DB rows\n  and config seeds) and `config/image-models.ts` notes — user data, not UI.\n  Since phase 2 the CALCUL mini-app is fully bilingual:\n  UI strings via the catalog (aria templates composed with `formatMessage`,\n  the tray aria stays stable AT CONSTANT LANGUAGE), énoncés via per-locale\n  packs inside `enonces.ts` (pools index-aligned and SAME LENGTH — pool\n  length is part of the PRNG contract, same seed → the EN translation of\n  the same sentence; digits-only fingerprint means a language switch never\n  invalidates a série), tray VARIANTES carry one phrase per locale on a\n  single shared pool (counts identical by construction), the A5 sheet\n  prints in the workshop language, and `saveMathSettingsFn` returns a CODE\n  (never a French sentence — the client's catalog labels it). Bureau\n  app labels live in the catalog keyed by the registry id\n  (`m.bureau.apps[app.id]` — icon and title bar read the same key). URLs\n  never localize (test:routes).\n- **Branding**: `src/config/app.ts` (display name, booklet footer/fallback\n  title) — set `VITE_CHILD_NAME` (build-time Vite var) to derive both, in\n  the UI language (\"L'atelier de Léa\" / \"Une histoire de Léa\", with French\n  d'-elision; \"Léa's workshop\" / \"A story by Léa\" in English via\n  `brandingFor(locale)`); `VITE_APP_NAME`, `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION`,\n  `VITE_STORY_LABEL` override the full strings in both languages.\n  `appConfig` stays the frozen FRENCH branding for not-yet-localized\n  consumers (print colophon, server fallback story title). Sample\n  heroes in `src/config/characters.ts` — meant to be replaced by each family\n  (they only seed empty tables; an already-populated db wins).\n- **LLM**: Vercel AI SDK (`ai` + `@ai-sdk/anthropic`), `generateObject` + the\n  Zod beat schema (see text adapter). Model from `STORY_MODEL`.\n- **Providers** in `src/server/providers/{text,image,tts}/`: text and image\n  are plain modules called by concrete name (`generateBeat`/`generateStoryArc`\n  in `text/dynamic.ts`; `generateImage` in `image/nanobanana.ts`) — no\n  interface seam (one implementation each, see the adapter-census note in\n  `types.ts`); only TTS keeps a real seam (`TtsProvider` in `types.ts`, two\n  adapters, env-switched via `getTtsProvider()` in `tts/index.ts`):\n  - text: `dynamic.ts` (the SOLE text provider;\n    required) — choose-your-own-adventure beats. Per-beat Zod schema (`title`\n    meaningful on the opening beat only, 1–3 short paragraphs — capped at 2 on\n    landing beats, exactly 2 choice labels or null on the final beat,\n    `sceneHint`) PLUS content guard-rail: `safetyProblems` (fatal — hero\n    named, narration never ends on a question, `forbidden-terms.ts`\n    scary/sad-term + stakes/evaluation-language scan, `sceneHint` included\n    since it drives the illustration) and\n    `structureProblems` (non-fatal — length/readability) → up to 3 corrective\n    attempts with problems fed back into the prompt (only a SAFETY failure\n    drops the child's saveur on the next attempt) → if the text is safe but\n    structure still off, `coerceBeat` salvages a valid beat → else typed\n    soft-failure → \"On réessaie ?\".\n  - text coherence (same file): a hidden\n    story arc (\"fil rouge\": goal → milestones → ending image) PLUS the\n    story's visual world (one-sentence illustration ambiance) are generated in\n    ONE call at creation (15s bound, best-effort — null never blocks the\n    first page); the arc is injected into EVERY beat prompt so the story\n    advances along one thread and the surprise element pays off. Each beat also\n    emits a `sceneHint` (where the action happens NOW) that the image prompt\n    prefers over the frozen place hint; prior beats' sceneHints are rendered\n    into the history block + a CONTINUITÉ system clause, so the new scene keeps\n    the same time/light/setting unless the story explicitly moved.\n    Structure guard adds an anti-\"doux\" repetition retry (>1\n    \"doux/douce/doucement\" per beat → non-fatal corrective rewrite), and the\n    last 2 beats get a `remainingChoices` countdown so the ending is prepared\n    instead of hitting the mustEnd wall. The same countdown drives the landing\n    DECRESCENDO (`isLanding`): the beats carrying the last 2 choices + the\n    final beat are asked shorter (2 phrases, schema `paragraphs.max(2)`,\n    non-fatal 4+-sentence nudge) — the story winds down because a beginning\n    reader tires by the end; the opening beats keep their 2–3-sentence richness.\n  - image: `nanobanana.ts` = Gemini image models, behind `IMAGE_ENABLED`.\n    The illustration prompt is assembled by the pure `buildSegmentImagePrompt`\n    (`image/segment-prompt.ts`, byte-identity golden-pinned).\n    Consistency: beats after the first pass the story's EARLIEST illustration\n    as an image input (reference) so characters/style stay stable page to page,\n    and the prompt carries the story's frozen `visual_world` as the DEFAULT\n    ambiance (the beat's own sceneHint keeps priority on location) so pages\n    stop drifting from day to night.\n    The reference is fetched server-side (10s bound); https refs are\n    allowlisted to THIS app's own Blob store host when the rw token is set\n    (else to `*.public.blob.vercel-storage.com` — SSRF defense-in-depth) and\n    local refs must stay inside the media dir. Any failure degrades to plain\n    text-to-image — never fails the beat's image. Gemini call aborts at 90s.\n  - tts: `edge` (msedge-tts, default) / `elevenlabs`, behind `TTS_ENABLED`,\n    selected via `getTtsProvider()`.\n- **Secrets**: read only in `src/env.ts` (server). Vite exposes only `VITE_*`;\n  all keys/LLM calls live in server functions (`src/server/*-functions.ts`,\n  story generation in `dynamic-functions.ts`).\n- **Generated media** (`src/server/providers/media-store.ts`, single\n# Env → DB settings — Inventory, classification & target architecture\n\nSession: 260731_1134_env-to-db-settings · Author: scout+architect agent\nMission: \"env vars should be set in the UI and stored in the database.\"\n\n---\n\n## A) FULL ENV VAR INVENTORY\n\nLegend: RT = runtime (server process.env), BT = build-time (baked into bundle).\n\"Frozen at import\" = read once into the `serverEnv` const when `src/env.ts` is\nfirst imported; consumers then read the const at call time.\n\n### Server runtime vars — all read in `src/env.ts` (sole reader, frozen at import)\n\n| Var | Default | Secret | Consumers (via `serverEnv.*`) | Runtime-change impact today |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | \"\" (required, boot-fatal via `validateServerEnv`) | YES | `text/dynamic.ts` (createAnthropic at call time, ×3 sites) | none until restart; frozen at import |\n| `STORY_MODEL` | `claude-opus-4-8` | no | `text/dynamic.ts` (beat + arc calls) | same |\n| `IMAGE_ENABLED` | false | no | `functions.ts`, `dynamic-functions.ts` (gates image fns), `getPublicFlags` → client UI slots | same |\n| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | \"\" (required iff IMAGE_ENABLED) | YES | `image/nanobanana.ts` (call time) | same |\n| `IMAGE_MODEL` | `gemini-2.5-flash-image` | no | `nanobanana.ts` fallback, `resolveImageModel` default in functions.ts + dynamic-functions.ts, mirrored to client via `getPublicFlags` (the /parents picker's \"par défaut\" badge) | same |\n| `IMAGE_RESOLUTION` | `1K` (enum 512/1K/2K/4K, typo-safe fallback) | no | functions.ts + dynamic-functions.ts → nanobanana `imageConfig.imageSize` | same |\n| `TTS_ENABLED` | false | no | `functions.ts` gate, `getPublicFlags` (\"Écouter\" button) | same |\n| `TTS_PROVIDER` | `edge` | no | `tts/index.ts` `getTtsProvider()` (call time — the only real provider seam) | same |\n| `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY` | \"\" (required iff TTS_ENABLED + provider=elevenlabs) | YES | `tts/elevenlabs.ts` (call time) | same |\n| `BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN` | \"\" | YES | `media-store.ts`: `saveMedia` backend switch (call time), `blobStoreHost()` → SSRF allowlist derivation used by `resolveStoredMediaForModel` and the image reference fetch | switching mid-life changes where NEW media goes; old rows keep working by the `/` vs `https://` prefix convention |\n| `DEFAULT_LANG` | `fr` (\"fr\"\\|\"ru\"\\|\"en\") | no | `dynamic-functions.ts:111` (story lang when wizard sends none), `getPublicFlags` | same |\n| `DATA_DIR` | `./data` | no | derives `databaseUrl` default; **`media-store.ts:21` computes `MEDIA_DIR` at IMPORT TIME** | changing at runtime impossible today (import-frozen); moving it would strand db + media |\n| `DATABASE_URL` | `file:<DATA_DIR>/app.db` | no (local path) | `db/index.ts` — client opened + migrations applied **at import time** | restart-only by nature |\n| `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION` | unset | no | `env.ts:83` (skips validation), `db/index.ts:35` (skips migrations) — the build-time escape hatch; also set by 4 test scripts | build/test infra |\n| `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` | unset | (legacy) | `env.ts:112` tripwire warning only — never used | none |\n\n### Build-time client vars (`import.meta.env.VITE_*`, baked into BOTH client and SSR bundles)\n\n| Var | Read in | Consumers downstream | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `VITE_CHILD_NAME` | `src/config/app.ts:24` → `childName` const | `components/bureau/portrait.tsx` (hero↔name match via `matchesChildName` + display), `brandingFor()` derivation | Dockerfile ARG + compose build arg; changing it today = REBUILD |\n| `VITE_APP_NAME` | `app.ts:31` | `brandingFor(locale)` → `__root.tsx` head tags (tab title), portrait fallback | Dockerfile ARG (not in compose args — compose only passes CHILD_NAME) |\n| `VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION` | `app.ts:30` | `brandingFor` → meta description | Dockerfile ARG |\n| `VITE_STORY_LABEL` | `app.ts:32` | `brandingFor`; `appConfig = brandingFor(\"fr\")` → `printable-story.tsx` colophon footer + `dynamic-functions.ts` server fallback story title | Dockerfile ARG |\n\n### Infra / tooling\n\n| Var | Where | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `PORT` | `package.json` start script (`PORT=3009`), Dockerfile `ENV PORT=3009` — consumed by Nitro node-server | pure infra |\n| `NODE_ENV` | Dockerfile | pure infra |\n| `DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS` | `vite.config.ts` (dev server Host allowlist) | dev-only |\n| `DATABASE_URL`/`DATA_DIR` | also re-derived in `drizzle.config.ts` (dotenv-loads .env.local/.env/.env.production) | tooling, must stay env |\n\n**Count: 15 server runtime + 4 VITE build-time + 4 infra/tooling ≈ 23 distinct vars.**\n\n---\n\n## B) CLASSIFICATION\n\n### (1) MOVE to UI + DB — 10 vars (env becomes fallback)\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `STORY_MODEL`, `IMAGE_ENABLED`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`,\n`IMAGE_MODEL`, `IMAGE_RESOLUTION`, `TTS_ENABLED`, `TTS_PROVIDER`,\n`ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `DEFAULT_LANG`.\n\nAll are parent-meaningful configuration, all already read at call time (no\nimport-time freeze problem beyond the `serverEnv` const itself). `IMAGE_MODEL`\nhalf-exists in the UI already (the /parents picker with localStorage) —\nthis work makes the DB the real home. `DEFAULT_LANG` is near-obsolete (since\nphase 3 the wizard passes the UI locale); store it as a DB setting defaulting\nto the UI language, env fallback kept.\n\n### (2) STAYS env — 7 vars (true infra)\n`DATA_DIR`, `DATABASE_URL`, `PORT`, `NODE_ENV`, `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION`,\n`DEV_ALLOWED_HOSTS`, `TURSO_AUTH_TOKEN` (legacy tripwire). Chicken-and-egg:\nyou cannot store the DB's own location in the DB; ports/paths are the\noperator's contract with Docker.\n\n### (3) TRICKY — 5 vars\n\n**VITE_CHILD_NAME / VITE_APP_NAME / VITE_APP_DESCRIPTION / VITE_STORY_LABEL →\nMOVE to DB, becoming runtime data.** Full consumer trace:\n- `childName` → `portrait.tsx` (hero identity match — `matchesChildName` in\n  `src/lib/bureau/identite.ts`, golden-tested in test:bureau on the PURE\n  function, which takes childName as an argument → golden unaffected) and\n  portrait display fallback.\n- `brandingFor(locale)` → `__root.tsx` head (tab title + description; the root\n  loader ALREADY fetches `ui-language` per request — same entry point works).\n- `appConfig` (frozen FR branding) → `printable-story.tsx` colophon,\n  `dynamic-functions.ts` fallback story title (server-side, easy).\n- The pure `buildBranding` (`src/lib/i18n/branding.ts`) takes `(locale,\n  childName)` — **unchanged**, so test:i18n's branding pins stay byte-green.\nThe mechanical change: branding stops being a module-level const and becomes\nloader data (root loader returns `{locale, branding, childName}`) + a plain\nserver read for server consumers. VITE_* stay honored as the env FALLBACK\n(the server can read `process.env.VITE_CHILD_NAME` at runtime; the Dockerfile\nARGs become optional/legacy). Cost: ~5 files rewired; gain: rename the child\nwithout a Docker rebuild — squarely what the user asked for.\n\n**BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN → STAYS env (recommendation).** It selects the media\nBACKEND (local disk vs Vercel Blob) and derives the SSRF allowlist host. It is\na deployment-mode property: on the family box (Docker volume) it is never set;\nit only exists on ephemeral-filesystem deploys — exactly the deploys where the\n\"DB\" story is different anyway. Making it parent-editable invites a foot-gun\n(flip it → new media goes to a cloud bucket) with zero family value, and the\nallowlist derivation (`blobHostFromToken`, golden-pinned in test:media) would\nneed cache-coherent re-derivation. Keep env; revisit only if a cloud deploy\ntarget returns.\n\n---\n\n## C) TARGET ARCHITECTURE\n\n### C1. Storage: extend `app_settings` (recommended) — no new table\nThe key/value table exists (migration already shipped, `ui-language` proves\nthe pattern), cardinality is ~12 rows, values are strings. A dedicated typed\ntable buys nothing here and costs a migration. Key naming, kebab-case with a\nsection prefix, canonical list frozen in one module:\n\n```\ntext:anthropic-api-key   text:story-model\nimage:enabled            image:gemini-api-key   image:model   image:resolution\ntts:enabled              tts:provider           tts:elevenlabs-api-key\nstory:default-lang\nbranding:child-name      branding:app-name\nbranding:app-description branding:story-label\n```\nBooleans stored as \"true\"/\"false\", parsed with the same tolerant `bool()`\nidiom; enums normalized on read (the `normalizeLocale` precedent) — a\nhand-edited row never errors.\n\n### C2. Settings service: `src/server/app-config.ts`\nOne server-only module, the single choke-point (mirrors media-store's design):\n\n- `getAppConfig(): Promise<AppConfig>` — reads ALL settings rows in one query,\n  merges with precedence **DB row present → wins; absent → env value → code\n  default**, returns a typed frozen object shaped like today's `serverEnv`\n  (same field names, minimal consumer diff).\n- **In-process cache**: cached promise + small TTL (~10s) AND explicit\n  `invalidateAppConfig()` called by every save fn. TTL is the safety net for\n  a second node process (there is none in prod — single container — so\n  invalidation alone is effectively immediate).\n- **Never throws** (getUiLocaleFn precedent): DB unreachable → env-only\n  config + server log. The child never sees a config error.\n- **Import-graph rule (CRITICAL for goldens)**: `app-config.ts` must NOT\n  import `~/server/db` at module top — lazy `await import(\"~/server/db\")`\n  inside the read function. Otherwise `test:coherence` (which imports\n  dynamic.ts under SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION) would pull in the db bootstrap.\n  `env.ts` keeps its pure env-fallback role and stays import-safe.\n\n### C3. Consumers become lazy (call-time) reads\nEvery category-1 read site swaps `serverEnv.x` → `(await getAppConfig()).x`.\nAll these sites are already inside async server functions/providers\n(dynamic.ts ×6, nanobanana.ts ×4, elevenlabs.ts ×2, tts/index.ts ×1,\nfunctions.ts ×4, dynamic-functions.ts ×6). `getTtsProvider()` becomes async\n(one caller). `getPublicFlags()` becomes async and reads the merged config —\nso toggling IMAGE/TTS in the UI applies on next page load, no rebuild.\n`media-store.ts` and `db/index.ts` keep reading `serverEnv` (category 2/3 —\nunchanged). `serverEnv` shrinks in ROLE (fallback provider) but keeps its\nshape so test:db's env-validation pins change minimally.\n\n### C4. Boot validation softens (deliberate behavior change)\n`validateServerEnv()` currently makes ANTHROPIC_API_KEY boot-fatal. With DB\nconfig, the app MUST boot key-less (first-run: parent enters the key in the\nUI). Change: key checks move from boot to point-of-use — story creation\nwithout any resolvable key returns the existing typed soft-failure (\"On\nréessaie ?\" already handles provider failure; add a parent-facing hint on\n/parents: \"clé non configurée\"). DATABASE_URL shape checks stay boot-fatal\n(infra). `test:db`'s env-validation golden updates accordingly (deliberate,\ndocumented pin change — not a regression).\n\n### C5. Secrets: honest threat model, no theater\nBox model: loopback-only, no auth — anyone who can reach the HTTP port IS the\nparent; anyone with disk access can read `.env.production` today just as they\ncould read `app.db` tomorrow. Plaintext in SQLite is therefore an equivalent\nposture, stated plainly in README. Rules that DO matter:\n- **Never send a secret back to the client.** GET returns\n  `{configured: boolean, hint: \"sk-ant-…7Yq\"}` (last 3-4 chars only).\n- UI: password-type input, placeholder shows the hint when configured; saving\n  an empty field = \"keep current\"; an explicit \"Effacer\" clears the row\n  (falling back to env).\n- Save fns return CODES, never sentences (saveMathSettingsFn precedent).\n- Never log values; the existing error paths already keep detail server-side.\n- README note: `app.db` backups now contain keys — same care as `.env`.\n- No encryption-at-rest: the key would sit next to the DB on the same disk.\n\n### C6. Seed strategy: PURE FALLBACK, no boot copy (recommended)\nDo **not** copy env values into the DB at startup. Rationale:\n- Zero migration pain either way, but copy-on-boot silently duplicates\n  SECRETS into the DB when the operator only consented to .env — surprising,\n  and a later .env rotation would be silently ignored (DB copy wins).\n- Pure fallback keeps one obvious mental model: \"DB row = parent decided in\n  the UI; no row = whatever the deploy says\". Deleting a row IS \"reset to\n  deploy default\", and the UI can show a \"par défaut (env)\" badge — the exact\n  pattern the image-model picker already uses.\n- No write path at boot → test:db's blank-dir boot golden stays clean.\n\n### C7. New /parents settings page — `/parents/reglages`\nFits the existing card grammar (the 🌍 language card is the model). Sections\nas calm cards: **Histoires** (API key, story model), **Images** (toggle, key,\nmodel — absorbing/linking the existing picker —, resolution), **Voix**\n(toggle, provider edge/elevenlabs, key), **Prénom & nom de l'atelier**\n(childName + the three override strings, with live derived preview via the\npure `buildBranding`). All labels in the i18n catalogs (`parents.reglages.*`,\nfr/en key parity → test:i18n), templated aria via `formatMessage`. Calm\nconstraint: parent-only page; no validation nagging — a missing key shows a\nneutral \"non configurée\" state, never red urgency.\n\n### C8. Hot-apply vs restart, per setting\n- **Hot (immediately, via cache invalidation)**: all 10 category-1 settings +\n  the 4 branding settings. Text/image/TTS reads happen per call; branding and\n  public flags enter per request through the root loader.\n- **Restart-required**: none among the moved settings (that's the point).\n  Category-2 env stays restart-scoped by nature.\n- One nuance: client-held state (the \"Écouter\" button, image slots) reflects\n  toggles on next navigation/reload — acceptable and calm.\n\n### C9. Golden-test impact map\n- `test:golden` / `test:coherence`: prompt builders are pure — untouched.\n  RISK: dynamic.ts's import graph must stay DB-free (C2 rule). Byte-pins safe.\n- `test:i18n`: `buildBranding` unchanged; ADD catalog keys in BOTH locales\n  (parity check enforces this); calm-wording scan applies to the new labels\n  (\"clé\", \"réglages\" fine — avoid anything evaluative).\n- `test:bureau`: `matchesChildName` pure, takes childName param — unaffected.\n- `test:db`: env-validation pins change (C4) — deliberate update in the same\n  chunk; boot-on-blank-dir must stay green with NO settings rows.\n- `test:media`, `test:routes`, `test:operations`, `test:reading-aids`,\n  `test:data-route`: untouched.\n- NEW `test:settings` golden: precedence matrix (db>env>default), boolean/enum\n  normalization, masking helper (`hintFor`), cache invalidation, never-throw\n  on DB failure, canonical key list frozen.\n\n### C10. Dockerfile / compose impact\n- Dockerfile: the four `ARG VITE_*` become legacy-optional (kept one release\n  for fallback, comment updated). `SKIP_ENV_VALIDATION=1` build unchanged.\n- compose.yml: unchanged structurally; `.env.production` may shrink to\n  infra-only. `.env.example` rewritten: infra section (stays env) + \"everything\n  else is set in the UI at /parents/reglages; env values act as defaults\".\n- README: first-run story becomes \"docker compose up → open /parents → paste\n  the Anthropic key\" — genuinely simpler than today.\n# Env → DB settings — Chunk plan for builder agents\n\nCompanion to `260731_1136_design-doc.md` (read it FIRST — key names in C1,\nprecedence in C6, import-graph rule in C2 are contracts).\n\nSequencing: C1 → C2 → (C3 ∥ C4) → C5. C3 and C4 can run in parallel\nworktrees after C2 lands (they touch disjoint files except the catalogs —\nC3 owns `src/lib/i18n/messages/*`; C4 adds its keys in a follow-up commit or\ncoordinates via the orchestrator).\n\n---\n\n## Chunk 1 — Settings service core (`app-config.ts`) + golden\n\n**Scope**: the server-only settings choke-point. No consumer changes.\n- New `src/server/app-config.ts`: canonical key list (design C1), typed\n  `AppConfig` (same field names as `serverEnv`), `getAppConfig()` with\n  precedence DB>env>default, one-query read, in-process cache + TTL (~10s),\n  `invalidateAppConfig()`, never-throw (env-only on DB failure + log),\n  tolerant bool/enum parsing, `hintFor(secret)` masking helper.\n- HARD RULE: no top-level import of `~/server/db` — lazy dynamic import\n  inside the read function (goldens must import this module without booting\n  the DB).\n- `src/env.ts`: keep shape; demote to fallback provider; SOFTEN validation\n  per design C4 (ANTHROPIC_API_KEY no longer boot-fatal; DATABASE_URL checks\n  stay fatal). Update `test:db` pins in the SAME chunk.\n- New `test:settings` script in package.json + `src/server/__tests__/\n  app-config.golden.ts`: precedence matrix, normalization, masking, cache\n  invalidation, never-throw, frozen key list, import-graph proof (importing\n  app-config.ts must not create a db file).\n\n**Files**: src/server/app-config.ts (new), src/env.ts, package.json,\nsrc/server/__tests__/app-config.golden.ts (new),\nsrc/server/db/__tests__/local-sqlite.golden.ts (validation pins).\n**QA**: `bun run test:settings test:db check-types lint`; full `bun run test`\nstill green; `bun run dev` boots WITHOUT any .env.local key.\n\n## Chunk 2 — Wire providers & server functions to lazy config\n\n**Scope**: swap `serverEnv.x` → `(await getAppConfig()).x` for category-1\nfields only.\n- `text/dynamic.ts` (apiKey, storyModel — 6 sites), `image/nanobanana.ts`\n  (geminiApiKey, imageModel, imageResolution), `tts/index.ts`\n  (`getTtsProvider()` → async, fix its one caller), `tts/elevenlabs.ts`,\n  `server/functions.ts` + `server/dynamic-functions.ts` (imageEnabled,\n  ttsEnabled, imageModel/resolution, defaultLang), `getPublicFlags()` → async\n  merged read (move it or its data source into app-config to avoid env.ts\n  importing the db — respect the import rule).\n- `media-store.ts`, `db/index.ts`: UNCHANGED (blob token + DATA_DIR stay env).\n- Missing-key behavior at point of use = existing typed soft-failure path.\n\n**Files**: the 6 files above.\n**QA**: full `bun run test` green (prompt byte-pins MUST NOT move) +\ncheck-types + lint. Manual: with key only in DB (no env), story generation\nworks; with key only in env, still works; IMAGE_ENABLED flipped in DB shows/\nhides the illustration slot on reload without rebuild.\n\n## Chunk 3 — /parents/reglages UI + server fns\n\n**Scope**: parent-facing page + save/read server functions.\n- Extend `src/server/settings-functions.ts` (or sibling module):\n  `getAppSettingsStatusFn` (returns non-secret values + `{configured, hint}`\n  for secrets — NEVER the secret), `saveAppSettingsFn` (zod-validated,\n  empty-secret = keep, explicit clear = delete row, returns CODES,\n  calls `invalidateAppConfig()`).\n- New route `src/app/parents/reglages.tsx` + a card/link on /parents index.\n  Card grammar of the existing 🌍 card; sections Histoires / Images / Voix /\n  Prénom & atelier (branding inputs land here but only take EFFECT in C4 —\n  ship the fields, they read/write DB now).\n- i18n: `parents.reglages.*` keys in BOTH `messages/fr.ts` and\n  `messages/en.ts` (parity + calm-wording scans enforce); aria via\n  `formatMessage`.\n- Calm: neutral \"non configurée\" states, no red, no urgency, no validation\n  nagging.\n\n**Files**: src/server/settings-functions.ts, src/app/parents/reglages.tsx\n(new), src/app/parents/index.tsx, src/lib/i18n/messages/{fr,en}.ts.\n**QA**: test:i18n + test:routes green; browse-QA: save round-trip, secret\nmasked after reload (response payload inspected — no secret in any response),\ntoggle image → reload → slot state changes.\n\n## Chunk 4 — Branding goes runtime (VITE_* → DB)\n\n**Scope**: design C1 branding keys + design section (3)-trace.\n- `src/config/app.ts`: keep `buildBranding` composition but source\n  childName/overrides from a server read with `import.meta.env.VITE_*` /\n  `process.env.VITE_*` as fallback. Client consumers stop importing the\n  module-level consts.\n- Root loader (`__root.tsx`): extend the existing `getUiLocaleFn` call to one\n  fn returning `{locale, branding, childName}`; provide via context next to\n  `LocaleProvider`. Head tags read loader data.\n- Rework consumers: `portrait.tsx` (childName + branding from context),\n  `printable-story.tsx` (storyLabel as prop threaded from route),\n  `dynamic-functions.ts` fallback title (server read).\n- `buildBranding` and `matchesChildName` stay byte-identical (goldens).\n- Dockerfile/compose: mark `ARG VITE_*` legacy-optional (keep as fallback).\n\n**Files**: src/config/app.ts, src/app/__root.tsx,\nsrc/components/bureau/portrait.tsx, src/components/printable-story.tsx,\nsrc/server/dynamic-functions.ts, src/server/settings-functions.ts,\nDockerfile, compose.yml.\n**QA**: test:i18n + test:bureau + test:routes green; browse-QA: change child\nname in UI → tab title, portrait, print colophon all follow on reload — NO\nrebuild; unset DB + VITE_CHILD_NAME set → old behavior intact.\n\n## Chunk 5 — Docs, deploy hygiene, release\n\n**Scope**: `.env.example` rewrite (infra-only + pointer to /parents/reglages),\nREADME (first-run = paste key in UI; app.db backups contain keys note),\nCLAUDE.md architecture bullets (settings service, softened boot validation,\nruntime branding), CHANGELOG.md (French) + VERSION bump, TODOS.md leftovers\n(e.g. deleting legacy VITE_ fallback next release).\n**QA**: docs consistent with shipped behavior; full suite green.\n\n---\n\n## FINAL QA CHECKER BRIEFING (end-to-end, after all chunks merge)\n\nEnvironment: fresh worktree, `bun install`. Use /browse (CONTAINER=1, own\nBROWSE_STATE_FILE/PORT per the orchestrator skill) against `bun run dev`.\n\n1. **Cold boot, zero config**: empty DATA_DIR, NO .env.local secrets →\n   `bun run dev` boots (no boot-fatal key error). `/` renders; /parents\n   renders; story creation returns the calm soft-failure, never a crash.\n2. **Settings page**: /parents/reglages loads in fr AND en (switch 🌍);\n   every label localized; no calm-constraint violations (no scores/urgency).\n3. **Save round-trip**: enter a fake then the real ANTHROPIC key; reload —\n   field shows masked hint only. Assert via devtools/network that NO response\n   payload ever contains the stored secret.\n4. **DB-stored key drives generation**: with the key ONLY in DB (env unset),\n   create a story → beats generate. Then clear the DB row with env fallback\n   set → still generates (precedence proof).\n5. **Hot toggles, no rebuild**: flip image/TTS toggles in UI → reload child\n   pages → illustration slot & \"Écouter\" button appear/disappear. Change\n   IMAGE_MODEL/RESOLUTION → next image call uses them (server log).\n6. **Branding runtime**: set child name in UI → tab title, portrait label,\n   booklet footer (print preview) update on reload. Unset everything +\n   VITE_CHILD_NAME env → legacy derivation intact.\n7. **Resilience**: hand-edit an app_settings row to garbage (bad enum, bad\n   bool) → app renders, value normalized, no error surfaces.\n8. **Suites**: `bun run check-types && bun run lint && bun run test` all\n   green — verify test:settings exists and runs in the `test` chain; verify\n   the prompt byte-pins (test:golden/test:coherence) did NOT change.\n9. **Docker path** (if the box allows): `bun run deploy` with a minimal\n   `.env.production` (no keys) → container healthy on :3009, configure via\n   UI, generate a story; `docker compose restart` → settings persist (volume).\n10. Report: pass/fail per item, screenshots for 2/5/6, any calm-constraint\n    concern flagged verbatim.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"The proposal is internally coherent, but several claims hinge on how server functions serialize data and how Nitro instances retain module state. I’m tracing those boundaries now, including the existing `app_settings` loader and media allowlist behavior."}}
